    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Green Street is a short street in the middle of our town. There are three shops on the street: a bakery, a flower shop and a bookshop. They are all small, and the owners know their customers."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Dan's Bakery is on the left. It opens at six o'clock in the morning and closes at two o'clock in the afternoon. Dan sells bread, cakes and sandwiches. His chocolate cake is very popular. A small cake costs three pounds."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "The flower shop is in the middle. It is called Rose and Lily. It is open from nine to five, Monday to Saturday. It is closed on Sundays. You can buy red roses, yellow tulips and white lilies. A bunch of flowers costs ten pounds."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "The bookshop is on the right. It sells books, magazines and pens. There is a small café in the back with two tables. Customers can drink tea or coffee and read a book. The owner, Mrs Patel, is very kind. She has a black cat called Pepper, and the cat sleeps in the window."
      }
    ]
  },
